#
# Path-based gosec rule exclusions for the ROOT module (core/ is scanned with
# no exclusions). One `<path-regex>:<G-rules,comma-separated>` per line; lines
# starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored. Both consumers join the lines
# with `;` into gosec's --exclude-rules value, so CI and `make ci-all` can never
# drift:
#   .github/workflows/ci.yml  (job "Security (gosec)")
#   Makefile                  (target _ci-module, MOD=.)
# Every entry documents a package whose flagged call is safe by construction
# (see the in-source comments at the flagged lines). Do not add entries to hide
# a real finding — fix the code or add a targeted `// #nosec Gxxx -- reason`.
testutil/.*:G115,G404,G204
search/typesense/.*:G704
notify/apns2/.*:G704
notify/fcm/.*:G101
hash/.*:G304,G401,G505
auth/policy/.*:G401,G505
auth/oauth2server/.*:G117
storage/.*:G304
secrets/.*:G304
docs/epub/.*:G304
cmd/golusoris/.*:G204,G304
archive/.*:G302,G304
webhooks/in/.*:G505
